Ultimately, I want to revise R/qtl2 to give NAs in these cases where a coefficient can't be estimated.

In the short term, you might replace the extreme values with NA.
Something like this, I think:

  co <- scan1coef(apr[,2], x$pheno[,65], kinship[2])
  co[abs(co) > diff(range(x$pheno[,65],na.rm=TRUE))] <- NA
  plot_coefCC(co, x$pmap)

karl

